 - 80ln(T/298.15)\nThis becomes negative when ln(T/298.15) = 50/80 = 0.625, T/298.15 = e^0.625 = 1.868, T = 557 K.\n\nSo at low T, both \u0394_r H\u00b0 and \u0394_r S\u00b0 are positive (endothermic, entropy-increasing). At higher T, \u0394_r H\u00b0 becomes negative (exothermic) while \u0394_r S\u00b0 eventually also becomes negative.\n\nThe condition \u0394_r G\u00b0 = 0, i.e., \u0394_r H\u00b0 = T\u0394_r S\u00b0, can have multiple solutions because both sides are nonlinear functions of T.\n\n**Part (3): K_p at T = 500 K**\n\n\u0394_r H\u00b0(500) = 38852 - 80\u00d7500 = 38852 - 40000 = -1148 J/mol\n\u0394_r S\u00b0(500) = 50 - 80ln(500/298.15) = 50 - 80ln(1.6770)\n\nln(1.6770): ln(1.6770) = ln(1.7) - ln(1.7/1.677) = 0.53063 - ln(1.01371) = 0.53063 - 0.01362 = 0.51701\n\nActually, let me be more precise.\n500/298.15 = 1.67701...\n\nln(1.677) = ?\nln(1.6) = 0.47000\nln(1.7) = 0.53063\nln(1.677) \u2248 ln(1.7) - ln(1.7/1.677) = 0.53063 - ln(1.01371)\nln(1.01371) \u2248 0.01371 - 0.01371\u00b2/2 = 0.01371 - 0.000094 = 0.01362\nln(1.677) \u2248 0.53063 - 0.01362 = 0.51701\n\n\u0394_r S\u00b0(500) = 50 - 80\u00d70.51701 = 50 - 41.361 = 8.639 J/(mol\u00b7K)\n\n\u0394_r G\u00b0(500) = -1148 - 500\u00d78.639 = -1148 - 4319.5 = -5467.5 J/mol\n\nK_p(500) = exp(-\u0394_r G\u00b0/(RT)) = exp(5467.5/(8.3144626\u00d7500)) = exp(5467.5/4157.23) = exp(1.3152)\n\ne^1.3152 = e \u00d7 e^0.3152 = 2.71828 \u00d7 1.3704 = 3.726\n\nWait, let me be more careful.\ne^0.3 = 1.3499\ne^0.31 = 1.3634\ne^0.315 = 1.3703\ne^0.3152 \u2248 1.3706\n\ne^1.3152 = 2."
